  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#input-modalities:-the-enterkeyhint-attribute\r\n\r\nFrom discussion in TAG review https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/380, given that the enter key is often going to trigger the submit action of the form, I'm wondering if this attribute makes more sense to have on the form element, rather than on the individual controls?\r\n\r\nIndividual controls could also have the attribute to override the form's value as needed.\r\n\r\nOne concern is if a form has multiple text controls but the author neglects to add the enterkeyhint attribute to all the controls (also simpler to manage in one place).",
